-- Generated by `pnpm decisions:seed` from docs/planning/decisions.md (decision 191): the log's
-- entries as decisions, numbered as in the log, active unless a later entry replaces them.
-- Do not edit by hand.
insert into public.decisions
  (number, statement, reason, status, decided_by_name, decided_at, origin, origin_ref)
overriding system value
values
  (220, 'Changes to slice 4.3 after an independent review, before it merged. The reviewer is given only decisions from the public log (`decisions.md`), cited by number, never those recorded in threads or found by listening, since the review is posted on a public repository. A review is written once: its text, concern count and cost are kept before it is posted, a later try first looks on GitHub for a review of the same commit with the checker''s footer, and marking it posted is its own step, so a timeout or a failed thread line cannot post or pay for it twice. Every attempt''s tokens are counted, each at its own model''s price, and a call that fails after it was sent is counted at an estimate rather than nothing. The posted text has no @mentions, links, images or HTML. A refusal, a cut-off or a diff GitHub will not send abandons the head at once. GitHub has no comment-only permission, so rule 18 rests on the code sending only comments; a machine user''s token is better than the owner''s. Before rolling the API back past this slice, pause or delete the `checker` job, which older code cannot read. The function''s time limit must allow a wake of about two minutes', 'The review found that private decisions could be quoted in a public pull request comment, that a post that timed out could be posted and paid for again, that some model attempts were not counted against the cap, that model text could mention people or post links under the token owner''s name, and that the Vercel type check failed. Each now has a test', 'active', 'the owner', '2026-11-26T00:00:00Z', 'import', '220')
on conflict (origin, origin_ref) where origin_ref is not null do nothing;
